ext} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72b0a8ce-efdb-5283-a1c0-67cde55875f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437726} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6da4c2f-c0a9-5c4a-b8ed-27e4c91a1921" :answer-field/key "$G = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7d2e918-eaef-52b0-bcae-68ce7040f744" :question/math-academy-id "q-125550" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $3\\times 2$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $E$ has $2$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $F$ has $3$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 2.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $G$ has $3$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $F$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e44ae12f-0b74-5b85-b272-52f6fe887a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462205} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f68198-6097-5921-84e3-218cc095e481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3f68198-6097-5921-84e3-218cc095e481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462206} :answer-field/id #uuid "9052a68f-40dc-53f5-bc24-4cb1f9880825" :answer-field/key "Only one player has exactly $10$ years of experience." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ebb57d0-682c-5af2-8879-12cb0e479260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462207} {:answer/id #uuid "d329c3da-4d09-578c-b937-1eb45e6e0c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d329c3da-4d09-578c-b937-1eb45e6e0c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462208} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a5413e6-6478-549b-bfc3-9a0cf468f957" :answer-field/key "There are two players aged $21.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a94125c3-5304-5a07-8e6e-a33a9346c736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462209} {:answer/id #uuid "759a777a-6a4c-5f2a-8f83-c615ee391bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a94125c3-5304-5a07-8e6e-a33a9346c736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462209} :answer-field/id #uuid "b57bc8e9-1d65-5f7c-838c-d3b9618b92bd" :answer-field/key "None of the players has fewer than $6$ years of experience." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c285e0d-9ca2-5d71-ae56-cfc30b5c536e" :question/math-academy-id "q-134130" :question/problem "![](images/bc/bc3809e55e601738d56be6885475ed442dec1fb3a0d2e19da14be045510f73dc.png)\n\nThe above scatter plot shows the relationship between age and years of experience of a group of professional soccer players. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement “Only one player has exactly $10$ years of experience” is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $10,$ namely, $(21,10).$ This means only one of the players has exactly $10$ years of experience.\n\n![](images/20/209759f5d70fd8587740d1da840f9da838a3c9a055a0d1e962f76c1cd6341fd3.png)\n\n- Statement “There are two players aged $21.$” is true. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $21,$ namely, $(21,10)$ and $(21,12).$ This means that two players are $21$ years old.\n\n![](images/75/753c503d6751363b1c7d2dc449f1c5f11baec159b1e938e8c807938512111750.png)\n\n- Statement “None of the players has fewer than $6$ years of experience” is false. From the scatter plot, one player has fewer than $6$ years of experience. The dot below the horizontal line represents this player.\n\n![](images/66/66facd1a0683f420aa2ac3d7bfd54290bdb009850bc66cc7523ee569ec81daea.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Only one player has exactly $10$ years of experience”; “There are two players aged $21.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092329 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a0cc5ea-7f70-5c5f-841e-01a6813da8c6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Operations on Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d1705b0-834b-5792-8c06-6d5fc22048b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448684} {:answer/id #uuid "b112adca-cb36-57f3-bd90-2e7a480434e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d1705b0-834b-5792-8c06-6d5fc22048b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448684} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ff8be7-384f-50f9-a9cc-07cf8d5eaf16" :answer-field/key "$P+Q$ is always a polynomial of degree $10$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449382} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af4bc898-dce0-5f3d-9d2f-6a7b8e8ffcf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448686} {:answer/id #uuid "b1aa0055-1d04-5645-beb9-c3d9eaaccc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af4bc898-dce0-5f3d-9d2f-6a7b8e8ffcf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448686} :answer-field/id #uuid "1841f66d-8716-5ae9-9721-03af6375e921" :answer-field/key "$P-Q$ is always a polynomial of degree $4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449383} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edf57af7-4b49-59d6-a5a9-3387654cc8df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448688} {:answer/id #uuid "2dcfac6c-2e42-52a0-9938-f9d8d1b51b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dcfac6c-2e42-52a0-9938-f9d8d1b51b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448689} :answer-field/id #uuid "d516701d-8778-510c-80b6-62bc3f31f92b" :answer-field/key "$P\\cdot Q$ is always a polynomial of degree $10$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c6cc47f7-3bf2-54bf-a0ea-9009aac01bb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-47447" :question/problem "If $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are polynomials of degree $3$ and $7,$ respectively, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$P+Q$ is always a polynomial of degree $10$” is false. For example, suppose $P(x)={x}^{3}$ and $Q(x)={x}^{7}.$ Then $P+Q={x}^{3}+{x}^{7},$ which is not a polynomial of degree $10.$\n\n- Statement “$P-Q$ is always a polynomial of degree $4$” is false. For example, suppose $P(x)={x}^{3}$ and $Q(x)={x}^{7}.$ Then $P-Q={x}^{3}-{x}^{7},$ which is not a polynomial of degree $4.$\n\n- Statement “$P\\cdot Q$ is always a polynomial of degree $10$” is true. The highest-degree terms in $P$ and $Q$ must contain ${x}^{3}$ and ${x}^{7},$ respectively. Therefore, the highest-degree term in $P\\cdot Q$ must contain ${x}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{7}={x}^{3+7}={x}^{10},$ meaning that $P\\cdot Q$ has degree $10.$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement “$P\\cdot Q$ is always a polynomial of degree $10$” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c85d222d-a0dd-512b-ade9-b7297ab2436e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439801} {:answer/id #uuid "4525f4bc-9d6f-5739-9cb5-120340760ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4525f4bc-9d6f-5739-9cb5-120340760ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439802} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7458e6a-4b2f-54b2-80e2-56d204005a2b" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440258} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d26baa8f-a5cd-56b2-8e34-1f62575bfed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439803} {:answer/id #uuid "715139b5-9162-5ce7-b651-d891134336f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "715139b5-9162-5ce7-b651-d891134336f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439804} :answer-field/id #uuid "700a856e-a911-5dd6-ba26-8d7a5387f9f3" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)$ exists" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92f1c0c2-09a3-5eaf-922d-4fdfc441678c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439805} {:answer/id #uuid "92aa5591-f4c4-5107-a4ab-d766d6df911e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92f1c0c2-09a3-5eaf-922d-4fdfc441678c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439805} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e44589-a032-5421-8508-b2a074b39704" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2832c750-5223-5055-a543-69f3bfc7bf6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48063" :question/problem "![](images/f5/f5ba5f7cc2ea5aaf405db1abff7e6f28ed4378ba6a5ec88d73c6861ede1d75de.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$” is true. Indeed, $f(2)=1.$\n\n- Statement “${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)$ exists” is true. Indeed, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$” is false. The graph of $f(x)$ breaks at $x=2$,  it's impossible to draw the graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85558fe1-9c94-53cd-9b06-9d10fd915bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439873} {:answer/id #uuid "41bb42a2-237c-50d2-bde6-1e67a38a37e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41bb42a2-237c-50d2-bde6-1e67a38a37e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439874} :answer-field/id #uuid "c62a73cf-8c33-535d-9dea-0086d3e41c0e" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty ,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440294} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dffdc7f5-2b92-5cae-91de-71f301a1f0da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439875} {:answer/id #uuid "528273a2-3a9d-5b9a-9b7a-08f3145a6a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dffdc7f5-2b92-5cae-91de-71f301a1f0da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439875} :answer-field/id #uuid "18169496-ec76-51fc-b481-2edec3fc6630" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (1,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ce25a91-38a4-5e06-8dbc-24d243e66ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439877} {:answer/id #uuid "1ae5b007-91e6-5976-a3c2-72321bebd9a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ce25a91-38a4-5e06-8dbc-24d243e66ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439877} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5c6a5b6-c726-593a-9362-e5d7e8c23832" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty ,5]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "912ff428-058e-5197-af7a-fcbe7f3d6387" :question/math-academy-id "q-66785" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-4|+2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-4|+2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $4$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-4|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-4|$ by $2$ units up to get $f(x)=|x-4|+2.$\n\n![](images/56/56956d0f23ae6828098507712fd00525dc4f114a195716dc16e63d8475e9c143.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,3).$  Indeed, on this interval, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on any of the intervals $x\\in (1,\\infty )$  and $(-\\infty ,5].$ On each of these intervals, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in (-\\infty ,3)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234403 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068695 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26385865-8d0f-55a1-bd86-65b238cbbe40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439955} {:answer/id #uuid "2ba5be98-ab6d-5eed-a69a-116bb223ca4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26385865-8d0f-55a1-bd86-65b238cbbe40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439955} :answer-field/id #uuid "69ddde7e-1a9e-5dae-9da9-7e3ff40034bd" :answer-field/key "$x=-7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ffcc78-4416-5f78-8eaf-65ba4096346d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439957} {:answer/id #uuid "94206a46-f33c-5db0-b3fb-83a6cfa82144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94206a46-f33c-5db0-b3fb-83a6cfa82144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439958} :answer-field/id #uuid "84fd6c4d-6e21-5efa-83f3-2ac9abfac29b" :answer-field/key "$x=-4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440336} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "743e9e46-5822-56a5-9b52-45a1659ac58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439959} {:answer/id #uuid "2248cefc-5075-52e6-bf71-0791631d6477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "743e9e46-5822-56a5-9b52-45a1659ac58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439959} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b6eb503-6847-5008-b6a4-9a6aec54ba5f" :answer-field/key "$x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9857052-b60b-5b90-a22b-cd84e32dabbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-78133" :question/problem "![](images/43/43544a1ba403055094cae54fed9772df353d3697f50888728ebee61e77b729da.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-7.$ Because there is a jump at $x=-7,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=-7$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-4.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-4$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-1.$ Since there is a break at $x=-1,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=-1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is: $x=-4$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "443c0bd0-2e77-50a8-91d3-a288d4ee852b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Order of an Ordinary Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b78f5f8-eebd-57fd-8d9c-03ba838f7aef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422279} {:answer/id #uuid "4c109920-c2c8-5c61-8b61-0f78d91253a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b78f5f8-eebd-57fd-8d9c-03ba838f7aef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422279} :answer-field/id #uuid "f370d4f5-a457-5b28-ac9a-80af2dd4a8a4" :answer-field/key "${y}^{‴}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}={x}^{2}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422420} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ef4fc5-634b-5120-a4df-e7cd35583cb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422281} {:answer/id #uuid "5957af20-d016-564c-98a5-0dad4377e784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ef4fc5-634b-5120-a4df-e7cd35583cb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422281} :answer-field/id #uuid "5817bd1b-3126-539b-b4d9-739ccf8be6bc" :answer-field/key "$5{y}^{″}{y}^{′}+3xy=4{y}^{′}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422421} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "084c63a5-b227-5826-b684-c0eef7a795da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422283} {:answer/id #uuid "265170ce-4178-5220-a328-3f5bd0ec833b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "265170ce-4178-5220-a328-3f5bd0ec833b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422284} :answer-field/id #uuid "224db637-215d-5076-9f8b-46454661000c" :answer-field/key "${({y}^{′})}^{2}-2{x}^{2}=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f506cb16-c146-566f-a58a-1f14b23b36b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-96669" :question/problem "Which of the following are first-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of first-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{′}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{‴}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}={x}^{2}y$ is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation $5{y}^{″}{y}^{′}+3xy=4{y}^{′}$ is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation ${({y}^{′})}^{2}-2{x}^{2}=y$ is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${({y}^{′})}^{2}-2{x}^{2}=y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "443c0bd0-2e77-50a8-91d3-a288d4ee852b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Order of an Ordinary Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equation I contains y'', so its highest derivative is second order." :answer/id #uuid "6fddfc61-ae75-5f4b-8b2e-b3415ea0d369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408168} {:answer/feedback "Equation I contains y'', so its highest derivative is second order." :answer/id #uuid "c834636a-bbd4-5759-b671-beb2e4da2abb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equation I contains y'', so its highest derivative is second order." :answer/id #uuid "6fddfc61-ae75-5f4b-8b2e-b3415ea0d369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408168} :answer-field/id #uuid "32f8bc9f-67ba-586b-b99e-1e38a930e19b" :answer-field/key "$3{y}^{''}+2x{y}^{'}={x}^{2}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equation II contains y' and no higher derivative. The factor y^5 does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "df851142-894b-5bfb-8ece-98c5eb3b201e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408171} {:answer/feedback "Equation II contains y' and no higher derivative. The factor y^5 does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "a4f9a0af-45e8-5e36-aa37-2b6d226dc143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equation II contains y' and no higher derivative. The factor y^5 does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "a4f9a0af-45e8-5e36-aa37-2b6d226dc143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408173} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d9436b-ef55-5798-a20b-5e6bc9ca9430" :answer-field/key "$5{x}^{2}y+3{y}^{5}{y}^{'}=4x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equation III contains y' and no higher derivative. The square root does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "1bb8cc3c-94ce-5d96-9edb-479fa67563b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408174} {:answer/feedback "Equation III contains y' and no higher derivative. The square root does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "6e1d4c62-4dd2-5856-8d10-6a84849ff212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equation III contains y' and no higher derivative. The square root does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "6e1d4c62-4dd2-5856-8d10-6a84849ff212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408176} :answer-field/id #uuid "495b552a-fc87-5ee2-b05d-892960260624" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{y}^{'}}+7{x}^{3}={e}^{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20db6c27-e8a9-50d0-bb54-61baf97c40e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96676" :question/problem "Which of the following are first-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of first-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation $3{y}^{''}+2x{y}^{'}={x}^{2}y$ is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation $5{x}^{2}y+3{y}^{5}{y}^{'}=4x$ is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\n- Equation $\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{y}^{'}}+7{x}^{3}={e}^{y}$ is also a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $5{x}^{2}y+3{y}^{5}{y}^{'}=4x$; $\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{y}^{'}}+7{x}^{3}={e}^{y}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "443c0bd0-2e77-50a8-91d3-a288d4ee852b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Order of an Ordinary Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d0d894d-c809-5dae-b04c-777fa7f1b329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422291} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef08266-c8b5-5d86-ba6c-38cec94b0b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d0d894d-c809-5dae-b04c-777fa7f1b329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422291} :answer-field/id #uuid "34bc34b4-9e03-56ed-af57-5921ddebb2d3" :answer-field/key "$3{y}^{'}+2x{y}^{''}={x}^{2}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422426} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccb30e5b-1e6e-5289-8a92-1d1a6eb3264f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422293} {:answer/id #uuid "5090af3c-f638-5321-a137-c61895760b06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccb30e5b-1e6e-5289-8a92-1d1a6eb3264f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422293} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b81d3a8-27c9-5a56-9c75-a52909222499" :answer-field/key "$5{x}^{2}{y}^{‴}+3x{y}^{'}={e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422427} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7601c375-892a-5f42-948b-dc68c11393c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422295} {:answer/id #uuid "4fae8008-076c-53ed-87cb-e76c044c94bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fae8008-076c-53ed-87cb-e76c044c94bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422296} :answer-field/id #uuid "a78a9497-be8a-530e-9cb5-154e8f8d6f0c" :answer-field/key "$4{({y}^{'})}^{3}+7{x}^{3}=x({y}^{2}+{({y}^{'})}^{2})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85cea071-187a-5be3-b347-b4aa26aead57" :question/math-academy-id "q-96680" :question/problem "Which of the following are first-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of first-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation $3{y}^{'}+2x{y}^{''}={x}^{2}y$ is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation $5{x}^{2}{y}^{‴}+3x{y}^{'}={e}^{x}$ is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation $4{({y}^{'})}^{3}+7{x}^{3}=x({y}^{2}+{({y}^{'})}^{2})$ is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $4{({y}^{'})}^{3}+7{x}^{3}=x({y}^{2}+{({y}^{'})}^{2})$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234492 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fa0c4b2-8dc6-5823-a9bb-b933a9f9ee7f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Ordinary Differential Equation is Autonomous or Nonautonomous"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24ca1a41-55a5-59ad-9001-0e2459c8bb6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422297} {:answer/id #uuid "e4011267-674e-5cd5-a96a-edbdb7f51458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24ca1a41-55a5-59ad-9001-0e2459c8bb6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422297} :answer-field/id #uuid "33de995d-3b57-550c-9c7d-aa966ecdaf48" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x={e}^{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b73cc998-84c0-5fc9-b67a-7c22e493f437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422299} {:answer/id #uuid "a43ee464-225b-5bac-b829-4893ccf7ec82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a43ee464-225b-5bac-b829-4893ccf7ec82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422300} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1f86d8f-f572-5fe3-9a19-500e72f3ef0c" :answer-field/key "$y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2=\\sqrt{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422430} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf0c55d7-5ac5-57f8-97e1-27c64bfea087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422301} {:answer/id #uuid "03394c62-f0fb-510f-ad01-72010e84b8a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf0c55d7-5ac5-57f8-97e1-27c64bfea087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422301} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6038821-1293-59ab-9ec7-324905ffa46c" :answer-field/key "$4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{x}{y}=5y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8cb765ab-56a4-5072-853c-55e0a9cdf71b" :question/math-academy-id "q-96702" :question/problem "Which of the following are autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x={e}^{y}$ is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x & ={e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{y}+x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)={e}^{y}+x.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\n- Equation $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2=\\sqrt{y}$ is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2 & =\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{y}+2}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=\\frac{\\sqrt{y}+2}{2}.$\n\n- Equation $4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{x}{y}=5y$ is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{x}{y} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{4}(5y+\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{4}(5y+\\frac{x}{y}).$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2=\\sqrt{y}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fa0c4b2-8dc6-5823-a9bb-b933a9f9ee7f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Ordinary Differential Equation is Autonomous or Nonautonomous"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232eaa66-0237-5dd3-a69f-3e3272efb858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422303} {:answer/id #uuid "11d01465-58b4-5e71-ad95-2ed8f89b7195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "232eaa66-0237-5dd3-a69f-3e3272efb858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422303} :answer-field/id #uuid "da09c621-2ab3-5008-9fd4-8147a7d93986" :answer-field/key "$x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}^{3}=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422432} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91da46cd-4fec-5066-ad81-e05c51f102c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422305} {:answer/id #uuid "73818976-acff-57a9-95f9-347242cb9a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73818976-acff-57a9-95f9-347242cb9a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422306} :answer-field/id #uuid "dceb4f87-957a-593d-8d26-547fd90cf20a" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-7{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422433} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d54ec6f4-81ae-505d-a857-5706b473527e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422307} {:answer/id #uuid "f81d0c2e-9ec1-5b79-942c-6f32380ff6f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f81d0c2e-9ec1-5b79-942c-6f32380ff6f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422308} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b0c1e47-f563-527f-b385-60bdc727eba0" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{ln}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ca7da4a-7115-52ea-963d-df4449aa6da2" :question/math-academy-id "q-96703" :question/problem "Which of the following are autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation $x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}^{3}=2$ is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}^{3} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2+3{y}^{3}}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\frac{2+3{y}^{3}}{x}.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\n- Equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-7{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{y}$ is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-7{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =7{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=7{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{y}.$\n\n- Equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{ln}y$ is an autonomous differential equation. We see that it is of the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ where $f(y)=\\operatorname{ln}y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-7{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{y}$; $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{ln}y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fa0c4b2-8dc6-5823-a9bb-b933a9f9ee7f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Ordinary Differential Equation is Autonomous or Nonautonomous"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0488ffaa-acc4-55b1-84c6-7107a1c151cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422309} {:answer/id #uuid "c67a1cca-c082-592e-8ecb-e3117b7bb71d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c67a1cca-c082-592e-8ecb-e3117b7bb71d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422310} :answer-field/id #uuid "064f00e8-e3b6-52e0-8529-c9f0f14fd0ce" :answer-field/key "${e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}^{3}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422435} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50501def-4ff1-5a98-9e69-d4d1e9355ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422311} {:answer/id #uuid "b69d5df5-08af-5c32-991c-9c15c44dd068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50501def-4ff1-5a98-9e69-d4d1e9355ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422311} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cdca183-2209-5d53-aefc-42d46c84ca21" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422436} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb6948d0-acc3-5286-8891-af6b60d2e31d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422313} {:answer/id #uuid "93a8855e-cb56-5720-b143-7887ce875bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb6948d0-acc3-5286-8891-af6b60d2e31d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422313} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fedbad3-4114-58f9-b8c9-fe8ec7b61ebd" :answer-field/key "$5x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "483de092-6fe5-5b9f-85ea-10c713e1d18a" :question/math-academy-id "q-96705" :question/problem "Which of the following are autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{′}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation ${e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}^{3}=0$ is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{y}^{3}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=3{y}^{3}{e}^{-y}.$\n\n- Equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+2x.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\n- Equation $5x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x}=0$ is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{5{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{5{x}^{2}}.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}^{3}=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fa0c4b2-8dc6-5823-a9bb-b933a9f9ee7f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Ordinary Differential Equation is Autonomous or Nonautonomous"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "486cbf20-6ed1-5ea6-919b-5e3452e6e684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422321} {:answer/id #uuid "aafcaf30-4b85-5f57-a825-f8813f70bba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "486cbf20-6ed1-5ea6-919b-5e3452e6e684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422321} :answer-field/id #uuid "466ce07a-3407-5b72-8d1c-b0b7154f1088" :answer-field/key "${y}^{'}=1-\\sqrt{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422441} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5bfc78a-3e28-567c-8ff8-90cd62f225d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422323} {:answer/id #uuid "c6099c92-190c-5449-992e-da3da0f24f7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5bfc78a-3e28-567c-8ff8-90cd62f225d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422323} :answer-field/id #uuid "aba0cf42-3e95-5a7b-8ea1-38a1d871a8d9" :answer-field/key "${y}^{'}-\\operatorname{tan}y={e}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422442} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e6bf198-bac2-537d-ac1b-b42144e1064c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422325} {:answer/id #uuid "084202a6-2162-54d6-9598-13a0685564ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "084202a6-2162-54d6-9598-13a0685564ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422326} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bad82c9-2c1b-5905-9265-70409b24568a" :answer-field/key "$x{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{y}=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad324671-5207-59c5-b2d9-048cb88806c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-96712" :question/problem "Which of the following are **not** autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation ${y}^{'}=1-\\sqrt{y}$ is an autonomous differential equation. It is of the form ${y}^{'}=f(y),$ where $f(y)=1-\\sqrt{y}.$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{'}-\\operatorname{tan}y={e}^{2}$ is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form ${y}^{'}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{'}-\\operatorname{tan}y & ={e}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{'} & =\\operatorname{tan}y+{e}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{'} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=\\operatorname{tan}y+{e}^{2}.$\n\n- Equation $x{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{y}=4$ is *not* an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{y} & =4 \\\\ {y}^{'} & =\\frac{4y+1}{xy} \\\\ {y}^{'} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\frac{4y+1}{xy}.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{y}=4$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31ed816f-dcc9-55e7-a7ee-b8893ddc6b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422345} {:answer/id #uuid "7c033af8-4e67-5059-a3d7-2ee152e006ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31ed816f-dcc9-55e7-a7ee-b8893ddc6b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422345} :answer-field/id #uuid "25e14789-c319-5f0e-bc5c-74e15f504fc6" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}{y}^{''}-y$ $=2x,$ $\\,y(1)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{'}(1)$ $=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422453} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "891fce35-cd60-5014-954c-b452492c406b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422347} {:answer/id #uuid "c19a760c-5182-53bb-9e1c-45300e79eda9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "891fce35-cd60-5014-954c-b452492c406b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422347} :answer-field/id #uuid "88417ad9-d92d-5c8a-9985-1095d72e3b30" :answer-field/key "$x{y}^{‴}-{e}^{x}{y}^{'}$ $=9y,$ $\\,y(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{'}(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{''}(0)$ $=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422454} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1015ba8-7c86-5225-bd73-031db89ebe78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422349} {:answer/id #uuid "7b79acea-a0fa-5455-a4fd-773c08b30342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b79acea-a0fa-5455-a4fd-773c08b30342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422350} :answer-field/id #uuid "a349157e-eeba-5e25-b578-93131466b86c" :answer-field/key "$2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y},\\,y(0)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85607d47-df50-5e10-bf9d-699a7a42f32f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96987" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{'}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System ${x}^{2}{y}^{''}-y$ $=2x,$ $\\,y(1)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{'}(1)$ $=3$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{''}-y=2x$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{'}(1)=3.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\n- System $x{y}^{‴}-{e}^{x}{y}^{'}$ $=9y,$ $\\,y(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{'}(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{''}(0)$ $=2$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *third*-order differential equation $x{y}^{‴}-{e}^{x}{y}^{'}=9y$ together with *three* initial conditions $y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{'}(0)=1,$ and ${y}^{''}(0)=2.$ This is a third-order initial value problem.\n\n- System $2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y},\\,y(0)=1$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y}$ together with the initial condition $y(0)=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y},\\,y(0)=1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8efe158e-5199-5887-8b3f-0d56b86243f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422363} {:answer/id #uuid "802b1980-87f7-5e28-9c43-ca80dce3ab91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "802b1980-87f7-5e28-9c43-ca80dce3ab91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422364} :answer-field/id #uuid "48575eb9-08b1-5ad9-be32-59c64f199db4" :answer-field/key "$3{x}^{2}{y}^{′}={y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422462} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b3fe1fd-a8ce-5d7b-bd4f-b4fbe96c661f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422365} {:answer/id #uuid "82cb1afb-17dc-54bc-9444-9e13f04751f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82cb1afb-17dc-54bc-9444-9e13f04751f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422366} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bffdb09-ada5-51cd-a74f-e8bfbb314c3e" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{{y}^{′}}{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}=y,\\,y(1)=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422463} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82a05862-f216-5d32-b34b-f327419d2f68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422367} {:answer/id #uuid "f8675194-82ce-500b-a188-7d2c2088e9ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82a05862-f216-5d32-b34b-f327419d2f68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422367} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5d5434f-556d-5bac-b0c3-5f61c1206ea5" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}-x\\sqrt{y}={e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e83e1ae-37f6-5806-9569-e87bd10cd10f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96992" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System $3{x}^{2}{y}^{′}={y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $3{x}^{2}{y}^{′}={y}^{2}$ together with the initial condition $y(0)=1.$\n\n- System $\\frac{{y}^{′}}{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}=y,\\,y(1)=2$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $\\frac{{y}^{′}}{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}=y$ together with the initial condition $y(1)=2.$\n\n- System ${y}^{′}-x\\sqrt{y}={e}^{x}$  is not a first-order initial value problem. We have a first-order ordinary differential equation, but there is no initial condition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $3{x}^{2}{y}^{′}={y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1$; $\\frac{{y}^{′}}{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}=y,\\,y(1)=2$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66f7ea98-35bf-58a5-b5cf-b3254eac5084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461135} {:answer/id #uuid "0bdc959a-7ea6-5e88-b4be-f14a882c4c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bdc959a-7ea6-5e88-b4be-f14a882c4c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461136} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fc286e9-461c-5f4e-8e2a-ce7ca85ea019" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f16fb85-a3d0-575d-9438-1840969bac72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461137} {:answer/id #uuid "e99d91b1-b055-5c0f-823d-6d6ff3dec609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f16fb85-a3d0-575d-9438-1840969bac72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461137} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee6e87c-88e4-5528-ba14-0dc349246406" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462322} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "628bdb8d-b415-5985-a3aa-cacb7f5d5e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461139} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea79588-ff3d-58b6-b8f1-64e70ed2b6b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "628bdb8d-b415-5985-a3aa-cacb7f5d5e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461139} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd1bc0b4-9998-5eaf-aa5c-1bd1a6d60356" :answer-field/key "$S={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68d1e936-89eb-56ca-bff3-c6afc2d2434a" :question/math-academy-id "q-100084" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2-2t,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(1)q(1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,2-2t⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{1}\\cdot (2-2t){|}_{1}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (2-2t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(1-2)\\cdot (2-2(1))+(2-2)\\cdot (2-2(2)) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,2t⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{1}\\cdot (2t){|}_{1}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (2t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(1-2)\\cdot (2(1))+(2-2)\\cdot (2(2)) \\\\  & =-2\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0ef9b09-f091-52da-9498-81b25acbb057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461141} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c27c63-9782-5dca-8e3a-f89ed5ced033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0ef9b09-f091-52da-9498-81b25acbb057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461141} :answer-field/id #uuid "481824b3-2e3f-592b-a547-b52518036348" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462324} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "440b28c8-ccdf-570c-94d8-a80cddfa6e92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461143} {:answer/id #uuid "07492636-38fb-5be2-a5fb-bc47855cd8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07492636-38fb-5be2-a5fb-bc47855cd8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461144} :answer-field/id #uuid "281d9ea7-7201-5f95-8dee-0cc341703d58" :answer-field/key "${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a65eb4c6-5adb-5c1e-ab17-ad96f89c6efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461145} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa75295-33ec-5de5-a6e8-187b0bb84398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a65eb4c6-5adb-5c1e-ab17-ad96f89c6efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461145} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d0c86fd-6c24-5d54-8ef6-ac2aaac69a47" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "794f079c-000d-5b83-a34d-0c1430e5e296" :question/math-academy-id "q-100089" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t-1,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=3t,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=1-t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t-1,3t⟩ \\\\  & =(2t-1){|}_{0}\\cdot (3t){|}_{0}+(2t-1){|}_{1}\\cdot (3t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(2(0)-1)\\cdot (3(0))+(2(1)-1)\\cdot (3(1)) \\\\  & =3\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨3t,1-t⟩ \\\\  & =(3t){|}_{0}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{0}+(3t){|}_{1}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(3(0))\\cdot (1-0)+(3(1))\\cdot (1-1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answe