p(-1)q(-1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t+1,3t⟩ \\\\  & =(2t+1){|}_{0}\\cdot (3t){|}_{0}+(2t+1){|}_{-1}\\cdot (3t){|}_{-1} \\\\  & =(2(0)+1)\\cdot (3(0))+(2(-1)+1)\\cdot (3(-1)) \\\\  & =3\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨3t,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(3t){|}_{0}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{0}+(3t){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1} \\\\  & =(3(0))\\cdot (0+1)+(3(-1))\\cdot ((-1)+1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bc79c40-802c-5928-96bd-62b5abc8ad53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461159} {:answer/id #uuid "624f3dda-272a-59f4-81c4-afdc89b1b569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "624f3dda-272a-59f4-81c4-afdc89b1b569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461160} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1795204-45a0-5ae2-b1e0-fe24f1661e9a" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462333} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d409008c-3927-5c03-9206-ddde6c3ce4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461161} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4f7f7d-e705-5bea-b85e-15ecc20591e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a4f7f7d-e705-5bea-b85e-15ecc20591e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461162} :answer-field/id #uuid "75ba454e-4199-5bbb-a3a5-a8496e22c83d" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ce821b-8ac0-57db-b8d9-ccfbcbc7d8fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461163} {:answer/id #uuid "3128022b-3800-59d4-aea7-1dbf26659f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10ce821b-8ac0-57db-b8d9-ccfbcbc7d8fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461163} :answer-field/id #uuid "104242d5-dc4e-5e24-ac69-a557c354d5fa" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e262e4d-a912-58d1-aa39-b29d3810a43d" :question/math-academy-id "q-100119" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t+2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2t+4.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-2)q(-2)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,t+2⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{-2}\\cdot (t+2){|}_{-2}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (t+2){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(-2-2)\\cdot ((-2)+2)+(2-2)\\cdot (2+2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,2t+4⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{-2}\\cdot (2t+4){|}_{-2}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (2t+4){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(-2-2)\\cdot (2(-2)+4)+(2-2)\\cdot (2(2)+4) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Let's check if ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t).$ Computing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t+2,2t+4⟩ \\\\  & =(t+2){|}_{-2}\\cdot (2t+4){|}_{-2}+(t+2){|}_{2}\\cdot (2t+4){|}_{2} \\\\  & =((-2)+2)\\cdot (2(-2)+4)+(2+2)\\cdot (2(2)+4) \\\\  & =32\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product. So, the set $S$ is *not* an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237797 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147492 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e71c0c9-7dd1-5f09-a55c-96b5bed1ee9a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Differential Equation Corresponding to a Phase Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49ec8218-3450-52de-b41b-a093639721ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461165} {:answer/id #uuid "921a73f8-3ee7-59fd-81bc-c93a9d997217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49ec8218-3450-52de-b41b-a093639721ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461165} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc424b5-73f5-5e6a-9116-73ba780ee733" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462336} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27885c74-a274-5c78-94e8-5552f9a71fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461167} {:answer/id #uuid "b099c22f-e7a7-5176-bfb9-76577a381d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27885c74-a274-5c78-94e8-5552f9a71fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461167} :answer-field/id #uuid "dedb7b4e-aa3c-5664-9589-a46141092606" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{3}-y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf4cc38e-88b9-5451-bf44-deba8b4ed1ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461169} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac205dd-a5bd-5d74-b4fd-b5f71d11d811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ac205dd-a5bd-5d74-b4fd-b5f71d11d811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461170} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b40d879-9d0e-596b-8019-dd8be3a85185" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)(y-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "74569aa4-36e3-5e4d-99a5-eeb148ed4156" :question/math-academy-id "q-100569" :question/problem "![](images/37/375647b4e2527841b48da5405effe2f15502f1d972586556796a55bcff441b94.png)\n\nConsider the phase line shown above. Which of the following differential equations could have this phase line?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all three differential equations are of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThe phase line gives us the following information:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=-1,$ $y=0$ and $y=2.$\n\n- $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (0,2).$\n\n- $f(y)$ is negative for $y\\in (-1,0)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's study each of the given equations.\n\n- We start by considering ${y}^{′}=-y(y+1)^{2}.$\n\nIn this case, $f(y)=-y(y+1)^{2},$ and the equilibrium solutions are $y=-1,0$ only. \n\nTherefore, equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)^{2}$ does not have the given phase line.\n\n- Next, we consider ${y}^{′}={y}^{3}-y.$\n\nIn this case, $f(y)=y(y-1)(y+1),$ and the equilibrium solutions are $y=-1,0,1$ only. \n\nTherefore, equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{3}-y$ does not have the given phase line.\n\n- Finally, we consider ${y}^{′}=-y(y+1)(y-2).$\n\nFirst, we see that $f(y)=-y(y+1)(y-2),$ so $f(y)=0$ if $y=-1,0,2.$ So, the equilibrium solutions correspond to those shown in the phase line.\n\nNow, we can construct a sign table for $f(y)$ as follows: \n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-1)$ | $(-1,0)$ | $(0,2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y+1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $-y$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $y-2$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is negative for $y\\in (-1,0)\\cup (2,\\infty ),$ and $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (0,2).$ This corresponds to the arrows shown on the phase line.\n\nTherefore, equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)(y-2)$ has the given phase line.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)(y-2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083201 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc6d9b69-0459-515a-ba7b-c62cab96ca00" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Divergent Improper Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff5263a7-1895-5085-8df6-00b5e700d455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461171} {:answer/id #uuid "6a138658-7727-5b84-9147-e75c4bc6f6be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff5263a7-1895-5085-8df6-00b5e700d455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461171} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fe9a7c8-6e85-594b-b112-88855ef364c3" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462339} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a49961ff-3ffb-57ca-a127-a6af05c42338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461173} {:answer/id #uuid "283b72c8-abd2-59aa-94d2-c526caba130c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a49961ff-3ffb-57ca-a127-a6af05c42338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461173} :answer-field/id #uuid "de28bf36-f83a-5fcb-b309-eca4f69c6915" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(z+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462340} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a089b8d-46c8-5953-a6f9-b2962253f826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461175} {:answer/id #uuid "ad3d8c52-3f24-5cde-b9fc-ebd2788b23f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad3d8c52-3f24-5cde-b9fc-ebd2788b23f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461176} :answer-field/id #uuid "292bf9b3-4412-5dd3-80d1-271235a3924d" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e90080f-3ef7-5c8d-a0d7-de79fffa1eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-101735" :question/problem "Which of the following improper integrals are divergent?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's work out each integral.\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-2}\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2{u}^{2}}]}_{a}^{-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(-\\frac{1}{2(-2)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2{a}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{2{a}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nFor the second integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(z+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{1}{(z+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{z+3}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{a+3}+\\frac{1}{0+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nFor the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|]_{2}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡a-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\infty ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral diverges.\n\nIn conclusion, only integrals ${\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x$ is divergent."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083201 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc6d9b69-0459-515a-ba7b-c62cab96ca00" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Divergent Improper Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11cbf150-b683-51fa-9f8a-d203bcfb3ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461177} {:answer/id #uuid "5956e27d-8d17-501a-8856-f798cc05f016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11cbf150-b683-51fa-9f8a-d203bcfb3ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461177} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c8fa3d2-c067-5b43-a12b-85e271c9cb1e" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{1}{(u-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de3cb94-3a2c-5891-aae8-6ea29f0d4df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461179} {:answer/id #uuid "8565509e-ebc2-5ae6-96ae-9d8817a43af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8565509e-ebc2-5ae6-96ae-9d8817a43af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461180} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f996994-3b27-587f-9d4f-5527cd7a6f32" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}t\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70ebaee1-04f7-54b6-af95-172ae288615f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461181} {:answer/id #uuid "4626a4f4-a591-579d-a987-b3940f00bbae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4626a4f4-a591-579d-a987-b3940f00bbae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461182} :answer-field/id #uuid "81f2e71e-76d6-53a1-bb19-e51bae15960a" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x-2}}\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30834ba5-7de3-5c58-8e09-a32166c98581" :question/math-academy-id "q-101738" :question/problem "Which of the following improper integrals are divergent?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's work out each integral.\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{1}{(u-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{(u-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{u-1}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1+\\frac{1}{a-1}) \\\\  & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nFor the second integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}t\\,\\text{d}t & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(0-{a}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{a}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\infty ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral diverges.\n\nFor the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x-2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x-2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[4\\sqrt{x-2}]}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =4{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\sqrt{a-2}-\\sqrt{3-2}) \\\\  & =4{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\sqrt{a-2}-1) \\\\  & =\\infty ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral diverges.\nIn conclusion, only integrals ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}t\\,\\text{d}t$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x-2}}\\,\\text{d}x$ are divergent."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "794398c0-ffbf-5971-a411-f236607f56b8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function is Differentiable at a Point Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2908bd70-c267-5463-a74d-0ddfe6c789d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461183} {:answer/id #uuid "95fd8294-3d0d-5c70-9232-f2fa78d7e2ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95fd8294-3d0d-5c70-9232-f2fa78d7e2ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461184} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf001b8b-ac52-5182-bdd8-d4318f82d9bd" :answer-field/key "The function is continuous at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462345} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d8be91-bdde-51cf-9ba0-8948cb045d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461185} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d2f2db-5444-5822-a897-5cc17a5f9694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5d2f2db-5444-5822-a897-5cc17a5f9694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461186} :answer-field/id #uuid "c11ab41e-9d76-550f-a331-7acf845c633a" :answer-field/key "The function is continuous at $x=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462346} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9c38ee3-ef2e-54ce-9483-f0f63a7c3597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461187} {:answer/id #uuid "1e3c1bac-aa00-5b1c-8a54-745d904ea141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9c38ee3-ef2e-54ce-9483-f0f63a7c3597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461187} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d578ca0-5c55-52ba-aade-9e39e8eee574" :answer-field/key "The function is differentiable at $x=10$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "016438b5-f9c2-5b0d-a1cf-02248bb802c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-101964" :question/problem "![](images/80/80fca5dc871cd083e638472abaf26b2a8ba91e81cfa5372df7398b4b63346dfa.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Statement “The function is continuous at $x=0$” is true. The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=0$ without taking a pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement “The function is continuous at $x=5$” is true. The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=5$ without taking a pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement “The function is differentiable at $x=10$” is false. Since the function is not continuous at $x=10$, it can't be differentiable at that point.\n\nTherefore, only statements “The function is continuous at $x=0$” and “The function is continuous at $x=5$” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "794398c0-ffbf-5971-a411-f236607f56b8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function is Differentiable at a Point Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ad7ef9d-6acc-5ee0-8cbe-2c445ee6e375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461189} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe63e74-5a8d-583d-a073-d909903628bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ad7ef9d-6acc-5ee0-8cbe-2c445ee6e375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461189} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9af70e7-f63b-580d-9382-7998be071336" :answer-field/key "The function is continuous at $x=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462348} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a1f9aea-858f-500c-acda-7a508c9ffa0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461191} {:answer/id #uuid "d3695edf-ea67-5c61-8197-e2046d6d8849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a1f9aea-858f-500c-acda-7a508c9ffa0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461191} :answer-field/id #uuid "507608ea-131d-5566-943f-d6991e34b29f" :answer-field/key "The function is differentiable at $x=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462349} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fc7f3bc-6079-5131-be86-1662d3ec264a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461193} {:answer/id #uuid "57c7df08-a8c0-585f-9280-89506d78dee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57c7df08-a8c0-585f-9280-89506d78dee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461194} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d2276e8-6e00-56fc-98dd-dbbff77f2df5" :answer-field/key "The function is differentiable at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08a8dbc9-b97f-57b3-acad-4c86f2f3f516" :question/math-academy-id "q-101983" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dc27a54ac20efc84bfbc404a20a91309c60c3fb42118f164129e93eee584437b.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- Statement “The function is continuous at $x=-5$” is false. The function has an infinite discontinuity at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement “The function is differentiable at $x=-5$” is false. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-5$ it can't be differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement “The function is differentiable at $x=0$” is true. The function is continuous at $x=0$ and doesn't have a corner point, a  cusp, or a vertical tangent.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The function is differentiable at $x=0$”  is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcbd56f-0fc2-59c5-a016-4272be4734c7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points at Which a Function is Not Differentiable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbfec55-9d50-5625-81eb-c98e80f3b8f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447648} {:answer/id #uuid "d74fc7f1-af07-5fd2-87d0-09768b3a5592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fbfec55-9d50-5625-81eb-c98e80f3b8f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447648} :answer-field/id #uuid "da028f60-caf1-57a7-b377-8c993930b26e" :answer-field/key "It is differentiable at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448864} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d4d0847-a963-5fa8-891f-6a48b17ebfbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447650} {:answer/id #uuid "ac85d7cb-70e0-541d-874b-6295040f6a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac85d7cb-70e0-541d-874b-6295040f6a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447651} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ea4398b-1044-522a-ab4a-e59e3e68e9ea" :answer-field/key "It  is **not** differentiable at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa585fdf-1bfb-52e8-a257-1b2fa75ef460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447652} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d1307f-bc54-5d72-b771-d51e3c5428d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4d1307f-bc54-5d72-b771-d51e3c5428d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447653} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b86057-34e7-5ab6-bfbb-8c7ca9adf67e" :answer-field/key "It is continuous at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0efb43bb-72c2-5796-b21b-537b0708d8ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-101995" :question/problem "Given that a function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$, has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$, and is differentiable at $x=-1$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Statement “It is differentiable at $x=0$” is false. Continuity does not imply differentiability. For example, the function $y=|x|$ is continuous but it's not differentiable at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement “It  is **not** differentiable at $x=1$” is true.  A function that is discontinuous at a point can't be differentiable at this point (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement “It is continuous at $x=-1$” is true. Indeed, differentiability implies continuity."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcbd56f-0fc2-59c5-a016-4272be4734c7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points at Which a Function is Not Differentiable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "063c39c6-60a0-580f-baa3-3b27a9b594a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447654} {:answer/id #uuid "60471443-2e4c-5682-a3b0-e035e11aeb30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60471443-2e4c-5682-a3b0-e035e11aeb30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447655} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d84fb65-64b4-5c74-85ae-5e31f4fb7cf7" :answer-field/key "It is **not** differentiable at $x=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448867} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea94764b-3418-54a8-a2ec-439a4ad572ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447656} {:answer/id #uuid "ed0cca5a-331a-542f-ae49-0505a12ce5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed0cca5a-331a-542f-ae49-0505a12ce5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447657} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94a5542-2aef-5d09-85b6-9d77a546b625" :answer-field/key "It  is continuous at $x=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "524b6e71-6f20-588d-b48e-0fdd95e218ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447658} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc9bbb5-5125-5baf-9d86-0e1b4e27ae02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "524b6e71-6f20-588d-b48e-0fdd95e218ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447658} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5275893-2258-53d5-a27a-ee98813d9462" :answer-field/key "It is differentiable at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5280401d-3d75-5547-be89-ad4f6f6c9526" :question/math-academy-id "q-101997" :question/problem "Given that a function $f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=-5$, is differentiable at $x=-2$, and has a  vertical tangent at $x=0$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Differentiability implies continuity. Hence,\n\n- Statement “It is **not** differentiable at $x=-5$” is true. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-5$, it can't be differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement “It  is continuous at $x=-2$” is true.   Since $f(x)$ is differentiable at $x=-2$ it is also  continuous at $x=-2.$\n\n- Statement “It is differentiable at $x=0$” is false. Since we have a vertical tangent at $x=0$, the function $f(x)$ is not differentiable at this point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068695 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d454d48-6ad7-52d0-ac60-83c0ac8f773e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437294} {:answer/id #uuid "14060581-f911-5f44-94a5-7b957230bdad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d454d48-6ad7-52d0-ac60-83c0ac8f773e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437294} :answer-field/id #uuid "6be63faa-8d5a-5a49-b394-4700822c7c46" :answer-field/key "$x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08caed72-8840-52c2-b454-83fc6d66acbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437296} {:answer/id #uuid "6f90d7b8-c269-587f-acdd-400474c83057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08caed72-8840-52c2-b454-83fc6d66acbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437296} :answer-field/id #uuid "8742df6e-f57e-5e1f-8e45-f5d4e42d35f8" :answer-field/key "$x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438677} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c250cd71-3e9e-5986-aa4d-df4401ae5a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437298} {:answer/id #uuid "f96ad967-28ee-58df-bef3-532adf94d6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f96ad967-28ee-58df-bef3-532adf94d6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437299} :answer-field/id #uuid "f10fa0a2-67c4-557a-b23c-de2310f1db3e" :answer-field/key "$x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3b92036-278a-5fb6-a1d2-39caf6b31601" :question/math-academy-id "q-102115" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d1d91b2d791d69c512a6bd2e7d523563de076a7f3afda53513234e799152ef8d.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-1.$ Since there is a jump at $x=-1,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=-1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1.$ Since there is a break at $x=1,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=3.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=3$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  $x=3$ only.\n\n \n\n![](images/57/57415045f7a1cc1c896756ff19cb17f90074151a25d12c56068fb6f86a064753.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237873 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115381 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b4100f8-8a66-5243-b0b6-c36b9d17dac3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Which Functions are Differentiable at a Given Point From the Function Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c3b4c87-9fab-59aa-9d2a-f9e5a0afd354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447660} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac28e11-2800-5b01-8189-b7f0e5bc5e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ac28e11-2800-5b01-8189-b7f0e5bc5e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447661} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd3cc92-82a1-579c-b6e4-5248b4cf9ea3" :answer-field/key "It is continuous at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4b274a0-5b0a-50c9-a6a8-9d8dfe49995d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447662} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea60c10-0347-5bd3-9342-6f9795ed1cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4b274a0-5b0a-50c9-a6a8-9d8dfe49995d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447662} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ae2668-47f6-57d4-bbcc-76b3461be81a" :answer-field/key "It is differentiable at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce2cc9d3-2885-5356-a0ae-008120301f4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447664} {:answer/id #uuid "1c753af5-0bef-5dd8-9558-8838edeaf903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c753af5-0bef-5dd8-9558-8838edeaf903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447665} :answer-field/id #uuid "1df32128-d223-53e0-9188-843aed6c8f58" :answer-field/key "It is differentiable on the interval $(0,2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6fe09a9-5d63-559e-a71c-67bb17b36b63" :question/math-academy-id "q-102163" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x-2, & x<0 \\\\ -2, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Statement “It is continuous at $x=0$” is true  Indeed, let's investigate the continuity of $f(x).$ It is continuous everywhere except, possibly, at  $x=0.$ At this point, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(2x-2)=2(0)-2=-2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}-2=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=f(0)=-2,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$ .\n\n- Statement “It is differentiable at $x=0$” is false, $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=0$ because it has a corner point there: \n\n$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)=2\\,$  if  $\\,x<0$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0\\,$ if $\\,x>0$\n\n- Statement “It is differentiable on the interval $(0,2)$” is true. Indeed, $f(x)$ is differentiable everywhere except at $x=0.$   Since $x=0$  doesn't belong to $(0,2)$, the given function is differentiable on this interval.\n\nTherefore, only statements “It is continuous at $x=0$” and “It is differentiable on the interval $(0,2)$” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "512f4d7d-a50e-5ac1-9b00-a23a2f1e85a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461195} {:answer/id #uuid "1be740a2-c20f-5fc9-8ec8-1f106667add1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be740a2-c20f-5fc9-8ec8-1f106667add1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461196} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3434df-a85b-5891-9fca-5190f4d5b98e" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a3ad9b-e804-5cca-a228-07b5c0f5b67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461197} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd91feb-5abf-5ad2-b1f4-c8b98678090d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50a3ad9b-e804-5cca-a228-07b5c0f5b67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461197} :answer-field/id #uuid "09fa150b-0bcd-5369-b4b9-9a606723ef7f" :answer-field/key "$AC=CA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc30d3d1-1efe-582e-944c-8f9d386f5738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461199} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd1d8db-a0f8-5a3f-9666-d01d5c0ea372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc30d3d1-1efe-582e-944c-8f9d386f5738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461199} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9afc227-2585-54bd-9518-4d409658168b" :answer-field/key "$C={A}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efd9ac2b-7a32-57f6-9899-3da1aeffaa13" :question/math-academy-id "q-102666" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ is false. As a result, $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $C={A}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3743095-b86d-5690-811f-9531139d1e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461201} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac7323d-37e2-59e4-a0ab-792785d6d9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3743095-b86d-5690-811f-9531139d1e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461201} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e0d85d4-3c22-5afa-997d-194a34f411f9" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462354} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1380862d-ca0a-5272-9181-d311561d8806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175