pply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $B={A}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eccb9532-7de2-59e7-a82e-6ab5c5c256d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461207} {:answer/id #uuid "a25d5fdd-a31e-51b5-a9cb-b9b85d9e48e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a25d5fdd-a31e-51b5-a9cb-b9b85d9e48e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461208} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a04379d-5