#uuid "ca4a88d6-0a16-569f-9ddd-9fa05f00f807" :answer-field/key "$C={A}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c9e4a51-c450-52e6-9d4d-f69fe8fdfc95" :question/math-academy-id "q-102673" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ is false.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ is true. As a result, $C={A}^{-1}$ and statement $C={A}^{-1}$ is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AC=CA={I}_{2}$; $C={A}^{-1}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a10723d3-f77a-5b16-956e-675d06c9d2d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461219} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b5ac11-5a94-5e5a-a683-6eaa4e645176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4b5ac11-5a94-5e5a-a683-6eaa4e645176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461220} :answer-field/id #uuid "b422ac1d-59ce-5d06-b337-6b4fb303c18d" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af232cd6-6074-5587-a841-b1542a97130d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461221} {:answer/id #uuid "334f6eb6-4b47-5b3c-8bc3-bb880538becd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af232cd6-6074-5587-a841-b1542a97130d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461221} :answer-field/id #uuid "511e276a-2d5e-5717-a6b1-f14915606998" :answer-field/key "$AC=CA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70774628-24bb-5d09-9ef7-435773771f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461223} {:answer/id #uuid "4971f816-a7a2-57fa-806c-3e7c66ba4153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4971f816-a7a2-57fa-806c-3e7c66ba4153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461224} :answer-field/id #uuid "305454cb-6946-5aa4-9b4a-f11fd3b2d954" :answer-field/key "$B={A}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98689422-75b7-52ec-a8b8-4a4a4c165a7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-102674" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ is true. As a result, $B={A}^{-1}$ and statement $B={A}^{-1}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & -5 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AB=BA={I}_{2}$; $B={A}^{-1}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec1398e5-e972-59d8-bca4-9aeed1536330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461225} {:answer/id #uuid "a135e004-34a6-5207-9ef4-ec52ff84fde2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec1398e5-e972-59d8-bca4-9aeed1536330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461225} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dcf6a9c-0fbc-5e47-87a2-e4afc24a5b1a" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462366} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b601a2db-1f2a-565f-92ec-73d330d6a3d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461227} {:answer/id #uuid "983da061-0c35-5c1c-b8d4-d3f6f57bf099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "983da061-0c35-5c1c-b8d4-d3f6f57bf099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461228} :answer-field/id #uuid "d871e3f5-560c-5117-a29b-84c94fa4deb1" :answer-field/key "$AC=CA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462367} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf901e75-aecc-5741-be79-99dbc17f48e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461229} {:answer/id #uuid "0fd87dc2-526d-51fb-9e56-db40d73cb638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fd87dc2-526d-51fb-9e56-db40d73cb638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461230} :answer-field/id #uuid "d13b0357-4115-5f8c-8d05-585642ecab89" :answer-field/key "$B\\ne {A}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7fa0b65-e3f9-5815-a23d-64900cd2d836" :question/math-academy-id "q-102675" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AC=CA={I}_{2}$; $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e961e28-39a7-5737-ac2b-099fbae2e86a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461231} {:answer/id #uuid "6a88879d-2697-5c85-a9fb-4aee80057dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e961e28-39a7-5737-ac2b-099fbae2e86a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461231} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3976f64-b706-5314-b304-45132d32f5ac" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462369} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bf63082-1a16-5959-963f-7181d938db36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461233} {:answer/id #uuid "4b63ac5c-6b0b-52d3-8316-1514510c3e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b63ac5c-6b0b-52d3-8316-1514510c3e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461234} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ee78f14-a2f4-5dca-81d0-b6a90c4b97cc" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462370} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d39ed48-ee3a-522d-8613-8dd14199bf54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461235} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd337af-ca50-58a6-9e40-ed9f475cfd7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d39ed48-ee3a-522d-8613-8dd14199bf54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461235} :answer-field/id #uuid "c92498fe-844f-5d91-b3e3-084780e00322" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "343b3c1e-da90-580a-91f6-9c9756fee1a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-103150" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+3)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-3,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $2,$ i.e., $R\\ge 2.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-5,-1].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-5,-1].$\n\n![](images/7d/7d68a4bd81717c3ad663fc85c45dfce62217a046f683cc92a6869f87ff3b166a.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=-5$” is false. Since $-5\\notin (-5,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=-2$” is true. Since $-2\\in (-5,-1],$ the series is convergent at $x=-2.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=1$” is false. Since $1\\notin (-5,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The series converges at $x=-2$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce59552-42d8-50fa-a897-42349ebc16b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461237} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb50c65-9777-5d34-aa33-37b64205dc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ce59552-42d8-50fa-a897-42349ebc16b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461237} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bb608e3-5b5a-5e3b-999f-d2563700f5de" :answer-field/key "The series diverges at $x=6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48763910-2d7e-5c19-a141-501b2718c16f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461239} {:answer/id #uuid "be4475de-8ca5-5c08-ac5b-ef0839ad6e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48763910-2d7e-5c19-a141-501b2718c16f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461239} :answer-field/id #uuid "04846c1b-e0e5-55ca-b43d-b9dac2441726" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d5145db-c8f3-5a11-bcac-ba051dfd7c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461241} {:answer/id #uuid "12406a8e-a857-514f-8e52-e7ec0c770dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d5145db-c8f3-5a11-bcac-ba051dfd7c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461241} :answer-field/id #uuid "f30ac93d-bc21-5c63-abea-26c7dd4ea0fd" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "21ccde81-8669-5255-b2ed-8bdddd923bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-103152" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x-5)^{n}$ converges at  $x=2,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=5,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=2,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $3,$ i.e., $R\\ge 3.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[2,8).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[2,8).$\n\n![](images/df/dfd59d22892764c4da387d48b07a6a1069ea59e13be75cd099d21ce53975d64c.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement “The series diverges at $x=6$” is false. Since $6\\in [2,8),$ the series is convergent at $x=6.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=0$” is false. Since $0\\notin [2,8),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=8$” is false. Since $8\\notin [2,8),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "753c6bc4-8bc9-5bc4-9b17-0e7b5a4fa7a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461243} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9cf866-8180-5637-bc9a-8cedd8a64adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9cf866-8180-5637-bc9a-8cedd8a64adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461244} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5e3870e-c98a-5c4e-b773-7c15a2ad964f" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462375} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f022f9a-3577-5071-863a-b61b2a5743ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461245} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2c4a3d-ac96-5582-8173-7504b99c0b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd2c4a3d-ac96-5582-8173-7504b99c0b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461246} :answer-field/id #uuid "96a988df-c939-58e6-bed2-1175955dc667" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "895d153f-7cd2-5072-b3ca-0e8cae1d45a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461247} {:answer/id #uuid "7de099d9-85b8-5974-a14f-c84279cd5b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "895d153f-7cd2-5072-b3ca-0e8cae1d45a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461247} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbcaf317-42fe-583d-9d07-58b3779f0c9b" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "93c0e2ef-7f5e-5e9b-aac8-f784a726661a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103169" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $\\frac{5}{2},$ i.e., $R\\ge \\frac{5}{2}.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-1,4).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-1,4).$\n\n![](images/d0/d01788625c7b429a15caf441c6a651fa92281dc544f99c544bdb12f9d8b6f032.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=2$” is true. Since $2\\in [-1,4),$ the series is convergent at $x=2.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=1$” is true. Since $1\\in [-1,4),$ the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=4$” is not necessarily true. The given information guarantees convergence for points strictly between $-1$ and $4$, but it does not guarantee convergence at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The series converges at $x=2$”; “The series converges at $x=1$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbe55739-eaf9-56ed-9d81-8e52c2ca8a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461249} {:answer/id #uuid "529614bd-8f87-5f2c-80b4-5c37e138c066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbe55739-eaf9-56ed-9d81-8e52c2ca8a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461249} :answer-field/id #uuid "c392bd2e-f2f9-5ceb-b0b1-f3a1b122ab52" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=-11$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462378} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54c50d44-335d-5651-ba10-b49f0f37fe9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461251} {:answer/id #uuid "61ae86b3-caf9-536d-bef5-f22c8cc87cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61ae86b3-caf9-536d-bef5-f22c8cc87cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461252} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce112048-db7b-58d9-ac72-bb8feec404bb" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=-8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ec3d05-89ca-5e41-af7d-d0230d5cab2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461253} {:answer/id #uuid "ace51aeb-e1da-564d-aaa1-10285b642108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ec3d05-89ca-5e41-af7d-d0230d5cab2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461253} :answer-field/id #uuid "72accc2e-3370-511e-9b00-a598c293557b" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "76850d0b-0e5d-5926-80f5-97253aff4b0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103170" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+7)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-3,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-7,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-3,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $4,$ i.e., $R\\ge 4.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-11,-3].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-11,-3].$\n\n![](images/47/4764256e5f00e7a11d688bd99d5fa1c22db819e7a188113f0ef4cd987a9b7595.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=-11$” is false. Since $-11\\notin (-11,-3],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-11.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=-8$” is true. Since $-8\\in (-11,-3],$ the series is convergent at $x=-8.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=1$” is false. Since $1\\notin (-11,-3],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The series converges at $x=-8$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147499 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Factors Giving an Exact ODE"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "090fc51b-4d12-5f60-88f8-ac5a4b13097b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461255} {:answer/id #uuid "4a490cbe-a1fc-5779-866a-04511c2d89df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a490cbe-a1fc-5779-866a-04511c2d89df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461256} :answer-field/id #uuid "4660fa26-6eb4-552c-b659-a5bb3fdb38e2" :answer-field/key "$3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462381} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203315ab-b883-5cf3-9e0f-dc0d51fd720c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461257} {:answer/id #uuid "2140d6dd-0dab-5e0c-9b15-f877af212e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2140d6dd-0dab-5e0c-9b15-f877af212e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461258} :answer-field/id #uuid "e00a579e-e820-57de-ab22-60410abdcf00" :answer-field/key "$3{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462382} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba813b06-d5fe-5f56-8fdc-f1ae37721250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461259} {:answer/id #uuid "19534c2b-71f9-5560-90e2-02c8041640df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19534c2b-71f9-5560-90e2-02c8041640df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461260} :answer-field/id #uuid "19628958-a21d-5f53-ae89-d685f932baef" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59bba89f-5fae-5f25-a8be-5a25060edfd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-103172" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\n2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $Q(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $P(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=0\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂x}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $Q(x,y)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y).$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))=0=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $Q(x,y)=3{y}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2})=0=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=3{y}^{2}$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1))=0=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)$ gives an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)$; $3{y}^{2}$; $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147499 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Factors Giving an Exact ODE"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6f503f6-69a7-5d68-a11b-13f00bdd16f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461261} {:answer/id #uuid "848dd2d6-6e77-557c-b98a-f43e6b7db9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6f503f6-69a7-5d68-a11b-13f00bdd16f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461261} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc41026f-42e8-5b54-9417-9d6b477e89f8" :answer-field/key "$6x{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462384} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f1fd05-76fc-5b99-a0c2-a90083805755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461263} {:answer/id #uuid "0f1f0dd1-4635-59a8-8716-ef1056569f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f1f0dd1-4635-59a8-8716-ef1056569f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461264} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b91d6b1-05d5-5e41-9dba-2acad420c227" :answer-field/key "$3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "106f08f9-0740-5a25-acd7-bad0545e6965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461265} {:answer/id #uuid "427fad5f-6fec-57c1-9ac0-73467afa5d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "106f08f9-0740-5a25-acd7-bad0545e6965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461265} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1e2b2a-3495-573d-8c25-cae8e1c5c279" :answer-field/key "$2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d411ceca-268e-5683-adfb-764387aebbdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-103174" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\n2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $Q(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $P(x,y)=2x{y}^{3}.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{3})=6x{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂x}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $Q(x,y)=6x{y}^{2}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6x{y}^{2})=6{y}^{2}\\ne \\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=6x{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $Q(x,y)=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6x{y}^{2}=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{3}{y}^{2})=6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\ne \\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''$3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ only''."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147499 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Factors Giving an Exact ODE"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6cba8d6-c415-53ab-badb-6bf8dbbbd0cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461267} {:answer/id #uuid "319d8d6d-e36c-5d92-9294-5c3e0ebc3a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "319d8d6d-e36c-5d92-9294-5c3e0ebc3a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461268} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d85e36-2f10-523d-8a99-52889142a7c1" :answer-field/key "${e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7b07408-8bfc-50ff-a374-c9d5ffa3c8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461269} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7fd223-bf94-5026-8a1f-ea7d0c2bf194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7b07408-8bfc-50ff-a374-c9d5ffa3c8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461269} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5efdf9e-1d50-589f-8cc5-55517cb057ba" :answer-field/key "$-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40734f81-131a-5471-b8b3-e03ea290a58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461271} {:answer/id #uuid "2a6b4205-de62-57e6-aad8-a56544ae9904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40734f81-131a-5471-b8b3-e03ea290a58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461271} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b089f27-1db2-55de-a28d-d2d13e8068fe" :answer-field/key "${e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ffb478e-6d0e-5395-bbb6-0e1bbace63ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-103175" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2})=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2})=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-2y\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''${e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}$ only''."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237982 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdd8d5ad-073e-55ee-92c1-3d941cfbf8cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437300} {:answer/id #uuid "62442bed-3629-535b-844a-f1ed8cc3a547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62442bed-3629-535b-844a-f1ed8cc3a547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437301} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b115472-4d06-5a5e-9cd3-15210c6010e5" :answer-field/key "The function is zero at $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7edfcf80-e21f-5e22-8902-7e7b1332485b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437302} {:answer/id #uuid "9c74c49e-6c9c-5bab-9fb2-8efb50f61131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7edfcf80-e21f-5e22-8902-7e7b1332485b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437302} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da1c4d9-8e1c-5e3d-8925-a2ad4ef01523" :answer-field/key "Its range is $y\\in [-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438680} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57a3617f-5ddc-5f1e-9587-578cb2e5daae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437304} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3927d0-6855-5216-a9b2-c6bb7f951391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57a3617f-5ddc-5f1e-9587-578cb2e5daae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437304} :answer-field/id #uuid "e42ef86b-359c-5579-8280-6358310897d5" :answer-field/key "$y=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is an output of the function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4817b633-1cdd-52d9-b9a7-098236a7867f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103230" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is zero at $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$” is true. At $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$, the function $y=cos⁡x$ takes the value zero.\n\n- Statements “Its range is $y\\in [-2,2]$” and “$y=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is an output of the function” are false. The range of the function $y=cos⁡x$ is $y\\in [-1,1].$ Thus, $y=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is not an output of this function."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54f7039a-2f3c-5e11-b655-d32aed6af515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437306} {:answer/id #uuid "d0e0e83d-6b7c-5018-bd20-49f606eedb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54f7039a-2f3c-5e11-b655-d32aed6af515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437306} :answer-field/id #uuid "e78118cd-b206-5d3b-aac4-77a392c6c22c" :answer-field/key "The zeros of the function are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi $" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fbfbd2d-9a45-5a4b-b854-d3e63ee7830d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437308} {:answer/id #uuid "0c07a39f-6574-5ab6-9301-59c89b690d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c07a39f-6574-5ab6-9301-59c89b690d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437309} :answer-field/id #uuid "62b3d79d-1762-5848-9642-6db59cbc38e2" :answer-field/key "Its graph passes through the point $(0,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438683} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efed1b10-8121-5609-a029-df7005434c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437310} {:answer/id #uuid "82200c6e-534d-5c90-9855-36c2db1fd8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efed1b10-8121-5609-a029-df7005434c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437310} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c76314-0f5c-552b-9634-7a579528542d" :answer-field/key "The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4afb86c8-970f-594e-bb88-36f6e2c3e725" :question/math-academy-id "q-103233" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The zeros of the function are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi $” is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…,$ which can be written as $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement “Its graph passes through the point $(0,1)$” is true. At $x=0,$ the function has the value $y=cos⁡0=1.$ Therefore, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,1).$\n\n- Statement “The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$” is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d62743dd-6b08-537d-99a1-950e0129a65b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437312} {:answer/id #uuid "ca6522af-a085-5421-9c2f-2778b4ad8bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca6522af-a085-5421-9c2f-2778b4ad8bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437313} :answer-field/id #uuid "7795f1b0-ab3b-568b-86a9-79ad8f59e765" :answer-field/key "The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62cebc6c-fb9e-5e2f-a4dc-892c8730f19c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437314} {:answer/id #uuid "7c865e34-f1b0-5ac5-896e-1465217ac529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62cebc6c-fb9e-5e2f-a4dc-892c8730f19c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437314} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a680935-e5c9-5bc1-9251-f1ef3483d3ef" :answer-field/key "The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1a71c62-3700-5f58-82ca-cdcc35abc891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437316} {:answer/id #uuid "f8103b2e-08e3-58da-8184-32ba8bfa5da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1a71c62-3700-5f58-82ca-cdcc35abc891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437316} :answer-field/id #uuid "895e53e0-0454-5c88-bc63-752876bb1bff" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2215b590-8140-5323-92bf-8ae24e1b7bb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-103289" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/73/732955302ca49a41f6c43cf242d7c869e630e88d804c4b56a5beb3b081f2d230.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $” is true. The function is defined everywhere, except where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement “The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n$” is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement “The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$” is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $” only."}]
